  "scope": "Unsealed descriptive scaling addendum using only completed reviewed60cells. No new experiment/productionpolicy/historicalcausal inference.",
  "paragraphs": [
    "The completed experiment shows a CPU/wall tradeoff, not a universal worker count. It contains60 separate cells across two eligibleCPU budgets, three workloads, GPU off/on and five requested counts. All480 native rows passed;120 warmups were excluded from the360 measured rows. Each cell has two fixed seeds and three paired measured blocks, referenced toN1 within the same workload, budget and GPU mode.",
    "On the six logical CPU mask, Playground GPU off N3 reduced wall by48.93% while CPU changed+2.13%;N6 reduced wall by36.53% while CPU rose58.99%. Oazis on that same mask had a different tradeoff: N6 wall\u221252.57%,N3 wall\u221249.48%, with CPU+39.16% and+8.19% respectively. These marginal ratios against N1 do not constitute a direct significance test ofN6 versusN3. They do show why a fixed-three production recommendation would exceed the evidence.",
    "Auto on the six logical CPU mask resolves to6, exactly as explicit 6. The six workload/GPU strata below show similar estimates with run-to-run variation; they are a count-resolution control, not a formal equivalence claim. Production remains auto 0 with the affinity-aware eligibility ceiling and explicit positive overrides. The experiment does not select a new default or infer the best physical-core/SMT/quota policy.",
    "On the24 logicalCPU mask, Playground GPU off auto 24 had CPU+426.84% [386.64%,453.26%] and wall\u221211.30% [\u221214.24%,\u22127.53%] relative to N1. Its arithmetic means were81.97 CPU seconds and13.79 wall seconds;N1 means are retained below. Extra CPU is not all proven waste: concurrent useful computation also consumes CPU, and the measured wall improvement remains real. Larger counts were not monotonically faster. Each budget stratum is paired internally; differences between budgets include scheduling/placement and experiment order, and are not isolated physical-core effects.",
    "System CPU and voluntary/involuntary context switches are observed process counters, not function-exclusive synchronization attribution. For Playground GPU off auto 24, system CPU per tick averaged0.002343 s, voluntary switches112.93/tick and involuntary switches0.143/tick. Near-zeroN1 switch denominators make percentage ratios huge; absolute values and zero-denominator qualifications are the meaningful companion. The forthcoming mature CPU sampler is a separate diagnostic and is not an inferred result of these counters.",
    "GPU on memory comparisons against N1 include count-dependent initialization and backend eligibility. SerialN1 and parallel paths can initialize/use the device differently; GPU on does not establish sustained useful offload. End completed/requested field counters are not GPU time, transfer utilization or chronological health. Do not treat the roughly doubledPG GPU on RSS at parallel counts as an intrinsic extra-worker allocation effect without that initialization qualification.",
    "The intervals are descriptive nested bootstrap intervals: two seed clusters resampled, then the three paired blocks within each seed;4000 draws. The tested initial windows are Playground20000 ticks, Oazis8192 ticks and large mixed4096 ticks. Whole process CPU/wall include loading, replay writing and teardown; separate engine clocks have different boundaries. These are not mature/end-to-winner curves, interactive-rendering measurements or nativeWindows/macOS/mobile proof. One host/two-seed evidence does not establish a global optimum, a quota policy or the causal percentage of any historical revision regression."
  ],
